---
import EditorialPage from '../../components/EditorialPage.astro';

const page = {
  path: '/development/',
  title: 'Web Design and Development Philippines | Bright Forge',
  description: 'Websites built by an SEO agency in the Philippines: WordPress and Astro builds, planned URLs and content, launch checks and maintenance after go-live.',
  h1: 'Web Design and Development in the Philippines',
  crumb: 'Development',
  byline: false,
  lead: [
    'We build and maintain websites that are planned for search from the first sketch: the pages the keyword research calls for, URLs that will not need changing, fast templates and a launch that does not lose the traffic you already have.',
  ],
  secondary: { href: '#build-steps', label: 'See how a build runs' },
  sections: [
    {
      h2: 'What we have built',
      html: `<dl class="bf-deliverables">
<dt>This website</dt><dd>brightforge.com.ph runs on Astro and is hosted on Netlify.</dd>
<dt>Shinobi</dt><dd><a href="https://shinobiseo.com/" rel="noopener">shinobiseo.com</a> is our own SEO studio brand for creative businesses. We built it with TanStack Start and Tailwind: a video hero with a readable headline, a manga-style interface carried through navigation and calls to action, and separate crawlable routes for home, cases, services, industries, development, blog, about and contact. It is our own-brand demonstration, not a client revenue case study.</dd>
</dl>`,
    },
    {
      h2: 'What we build with',
      html: `<dl class="bf-deliverables">
<dt><a href="/development/wordpress/">WordPress</a></dt><dd>When your team needs to edit pages and publish without a developer.</dd>
<dt><a href="/development/astro/">Astro</a></dt><dd>For content-led sites where speed matters and the pages change less often.</dd>
<dt>React-based frameworks</dt><dd>Such as Next.js or TanStack Start, for sites that are partly applications: dashboards, booking tools, product configurators. Shinobi is built this way.</dd>
</dl>
<p>We recommend the simplest platform that does the job. Most business websites do not need a JavaScript framework.</p>`,
    },
    {
      h2: 'How a build runs, step by step',
      id: 'build-steps',
      html: `<ol class="bf-steps">
<li><strong>Audit</strong> of the existing site: what ranks, what converts, what must be kept.</li>
<li><strong>Plan:</strong> page list from keyword research, URL structure, redirect map, content plan.</li>
<li><strong>Design</strong> on real content.</li>
<li><strong>Build</strong>, on a preview you can test at phone and desktop sizes.</li>
<li><strong>Pre-launch checks:</strong> every page has a title, one H1, a canonical and correct indexing rules; redirects tested; forms and tracking tested; speed measured on a phone.</li>
<li><strong>Launch and monitoring.</strong> We read the public pages and test the agreed links and forms after deployment.</li>
<li><strong>Handover:</strong> a clear record of what was built, and agreement on who owns updates, backups, CMS access and hosting accounts.</li>
</ol>
<p>Where the build replaces an existing site, the redirect and launch work is covered by our <a href="/website-migration-services/">website migration services</a>, and <a href="/technical-seo-services-philippines/">technical SEO</a> checks the result.</p>`,
    },
    {
      h2: 'Maintenance',
      html: `<p>After launch we can keep maintaining the site. What is covered, the monitoring period and the response times are set in the proposal; they are not assumed.</p>`,
    },
    {
      h2: 'Pricing',
      html: `<p>Each build is quoted in a private proposal. There is no public rate card: the scope depends on the size of the site, the design, how ready the content is, integrations, the platform, migration requirements and testing. Our article on <a href="/blog/what-a-website-costs-in-the-philippines/">what a website costs in the Philippines</a> explains what moves the figure.</p>`,
    },
  ],
  faqs: [
    { question: 'Can you redesign our site without losing rankings?', answer: 'That is the purpose of the audit, the plan and the pre-launch checks. Ranking movement can still occur after a carefully tested rebuild. See <a href="/website-migration-services/">website migration services</a>.' },
    { question: 'Will we be able to edit the site ourselves?', answer: 'On WordPress, yes: your team can edit pages without a deploy. On an Astro build, we agree before choosing it who will make content changes and how.' },
    { question: 'Will the site be responsive?', answer: 'Yes. Phone, tablet and desktop are part of the design, not a leftover stylesheet. We test the enquiry path on a phone before we call a layout done.' },
  ],
  contact: { h2: 'Planning a build? Request a review', text: 'Send the current site, or the brief if there is none yet, and what the new site has to do. We usually reply within one business day.' },
};
---
<EditorialPage page={page} />
